<%# FUIME: written for a 13-to-17-year-old whose earnings just went down, and
    who did nothing wrong.

    Three rules this copy is built on:
      * No bank vocabulary (L5). What moved is what Fuime owes them, not a
        balance held anywhere.
      * No action is asked for, because there is none — Fuime is the seller of
        record and Fuime answers the dispute. Asking a minor to "respond" would
        be both false and alarming.
      * Say what happens next and when, so the number on their page has an
        explanation attached to it. %>

<p>Hi,</p>

<p>
  A customer asked their card company to reverse a payment they made to
  <strong><%= @event.name %></strong>. This is called a dispute, or a chargeback.
</p>

<p>
  While it is being reviewed, <strong><%= render_money @dispute.amount_cents %></strong>
  has been taken off what Fuime owes you for that sale. That is why the amount on
  your payouts page changed.
</p>

<p>
  <strong>You do not need to do anything.</strong> Fuime is the legal seller on
  every sale made through the platform, so the card company's dispute is with
  Fuime and we handle the response. If we win it, the amount goes back to what
  you are owed. If we lose it, it stays reduced — that is the part of selling
  online that we carry with you.
</p>

<p>
  If you know something about this sale that would help — what you delivered,
  when, and any messages with the customer — reply to this email and it will
  reach a person. It genuinely helps.
</p>

<p><%= link_to "Your payouts page", @payouts_url %></p>

<p>
  Questions: <%= mail_to @support_email %>
</p>
